SUMMARY:linkedin: The drawer of old drives
DESCRIPTION:DRAFT — importing this event does not schedule a social pos
 t.\nAsset: graphics/P02.png\n\nAn old laptop drive. A disk labelled “ba
 ckup”. Another labelled “backup old”.\n\nThe hard part of sorting t
 hem is often knowing what each one contains. Which folders came from the 
 same computer? Which hold something you still need? Which have another co
 py?\n\nBackDown began with a real drive-consolidation job: years of old d
 isks needed to become one archive. That experience still shapes the produ
 ct.\n\nThe current alpha can index a drive and let you browse the invento
 ry locally. Hashing and duplicate checks add evidence about matching cont
 ent across the drives you have indexed.\n\nThe next time you plug in a fo
 rgotten drive\, start by finding out what is there. Join early access for
  one email when BackDown is ready.\n\nhttps://backdown.io/?utm_source=lin
 kedin&utm_medium=organic_social&utm_campaign=bd_launch_2026_09&utm_conten
 t=p02#join\n\nPublication conditions (not part of the post):\nReview fina
 l copy and current release status.
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
