BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:P04-hacker_news@backdown.io
DTSTAMP:20260928T120000Z
DTSTART:20261006T153000Z
DTEND:20261006T173000Z
SUMMARY:[Optional / conditional] hacker_news: Show HN launch
DESCRIPTION:DRAFT — importing this event does not schedule a social pos
 t.\nAsset: \n\nShow HN: BackDown – local drive inventory and hash-based
  duplicate checks\n\nSubmission URL: https://backdown.io/download/?utm_so
 urce=hacker_news&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bd_launch_2026_09&utm_c
 ontent=show_hn\n\nI’m working on BackDown\, a local drive-inventory and
  duplicate-checking tool.\n\nBackDown began as a one-off job to consolida
 te years of old drives into one archive. The original scripts indexed abo
 ut 27 million files and read and hashed 15 TB in that founding dataset. T
 hose numbers describe that particular archive\, not a general performance
  claim.\n\nThe current public build is v0.2.0-alpha.4. It provides index\
 , hash\, dupes and check commands\, plus a local browser and read-only vi
 ewers for supported files. Builds cover Linux x86-64 and ARM64\, macOS un
 iversal\, and Windows x86-64.\n\nDownload and setup notes: https://backdo
 wn.io/download/\n\nThere is no signup gate. The local edition needs no ac
 count and sends no telemetry. This is an early alpha\, rather than the pl
 anned polished native desktop release. Broader planning and copying workf
 lows are still roadmap work.\n\nUseful feedback would include confusing i
 nventory results\, content comparisons that need more explanation\, and r
 eproducible browser or viewer problems. Please use non-sensitive examples
 \; sharing a private archive is not necessary.\n\nPublication conditions 
 (not part of the post):\nCurrent public CLI download and installation hav
 e been verified immediately before submission.\nThe author is free to rep
 ly for at least two hours after submission.\nThe submission links directl
 y to /download/ and requires no signup to try the product.
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
