BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:P11-linkedin@backdown.io
DTSTAMP:20260928T120000Z
DTSTART:20261022T083000Z
DTEND:20261022T085000Z
SUMMARY:linkedin: Names do not prove content
DESCRIPTION:DRAFT — importing this event does not schedule a social pos
 t.\nAsset: graphics/P11.png\n\nConsider two files both named “holiday.j
 pg”. They could be different photos.\n\nNow consider “holiday.jpg” 
 and “holiday-copy.jpg”. They could contain exactly the same photo dat
 a.\n\nNames help people organise things\, but they do not establish that 
 file contents match. That becomes a problem when years of exports\, renam
 ed folders and device backups meet in one archive.\n\nBackDown's alpha us
 es content hashing as part of its duplicate checks. It helps you investig
 ate copies by their data\, while keeping the paths available so you can u
 nderstand where the results came from.\n\nA match is still something to i
 nterpret within your backup plan. Start with evidence\, then decide which
  copies serve a purpose.\n\nJoin early access for one email when BackDown
  is ready.\n\nhttps://backdown.io/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=organic
 _social&utm_campaign=bd_launch_2026_09&utm_content=p11#join\n\nPublicatio
 n conditions (not part of the post):\nReview final copy and current relea
 se status.
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
